SUMMARY:Panigiri of Ai-Giannis Siderianos\, Chalakas
LOCATION:Chalakas\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The last big feast of the Milos season\, for Agios Ioannis Theologos 'Siderianos' at the old monastery in the wild south-west (Chalakas). The icon is brought over from the Korfiatissa church with honours\, and the village and the church committee lay on a glenti with island musicians in the courtyard\; the party is usually held on the Saturday nearest the feast (20 Sept 2025\, 21 Sept 2024) with vespers on 25 September\, so check milosvoice.gr for the exact night. Hundreds come\, including Kimolians\; the road in is unpaved for the last stretch.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#chalakas-panigiri-of-ai-giannis-siderianos-chalakas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#chalakas-panigiri-of-ai-giannis-siderianos-chalakas
